WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.293
Relevance is more than adding a workplace photograph.

00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:09.013
In this sample, it means practicing the decision that creates a usable handoff.

00:00:09.253 --> 00:00:16.336
Motivation may include doing useful work, confidence, recognition, or simply meeting an employment requirement.

00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:21.205
Do not assume everyone arrives enthusiastic or motivated in the same way.

00:00:21.895 --> 00:00:31.351
Worked example: replace a long department history with a short opening: “By the end, you will choose an owner and next action for a handoff so another

00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:36.871
agent can continue the case.” Let learners select a password-reset or order-status case.

00:00:37.111 --> 00:00:40.994
Both use the same required fields and performance criterion.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:46.205
Offer a text example, optional demonstration, and a readily available checklist.

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:54.103
These options support access and task needs; they do not label people as fixed visual, auditory, or kinesthetic learners.

00:00:54.793 --> 00:00:56.073
Choice has boundaries.

00:00:56.313 --> 00:01:02.500
A learner may choose a relevant practice case, but cannot skip a required safety or privacy control.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:08.116
An experienced user may need less explanation, while a novice may need the complete walkthrough.

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:12.175
Check performance rather than relying only on confidence ratings.

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:18.646
Mini-design task: choose a workplace example for a novice and one for an experienced colleague.

00:01:18.886 --> 00:01:21.062
Keep the assessed requirement identical.

00:01:21.302 --> 00:01:24.886
Write one sentence explaining why each example is relevant.

00:01:25.576 --> 00:01:26.664
Now it's your turn.

00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:30.211
You have novices and experienced agents in one session.

00:01:30.451 --> 00:01:33.864
Which plan best balances choice and common expectations?

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:37.219
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

